  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Margaret is studying and analyzing a culture of bacteria. From a certain moment, she notices that the number of bacteria $B(t)$ in the culture grows according to the formula $B(t)=500\\cdot {2}^{t},$ where $t$ denotes the time in hours. How many bacteria will there be after $4$ hours?",
  "worked_solution": "To get the number of bacteria in the culture after $4$ hours, we evaluate the function at $t=4.$ Substituting $t=4$ into the function $B(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =500\\cdot (2)^{(4)} \\\\  & =500\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =8\\,000.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there will be $8\\,000$ bacteria in the culture after $4$ hours.",
